# Redirects for static assets (SPEC §7.2, §18.2). The build copies this file
# to dist/_redirects; Wrangler reads it as config and never serves it. One
# rule a line: source, destination, status. A line Cloudflare can't read is
# dropped with only a warning in the build log, so
# test/node/deploy-config.test.js checks every line.

# The Sleep problems page is part of the home page since 2026-11-13 (SPEC
# §22), so its old address goes there. A rule with no * matches only the
# exact path it names, so the address is listed with and without its final
# slash, and neither rule matches a problem page (/problems/<slug>/).
# Browsers keep a #fragment across a redirect, so /problems/#core arrives at
# /#core, where that area opens.
/problems / 301
/problems/ / 301
